:"Text"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"},{"config":{"align":"end","direction":"vertical","gap":8,"justify":"end","overlay":true,"padding":16},"id":"tray","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"direction":"vertical","maxWidth":"100%","visible":false,"width":"360px"},"id":"toast-locale-wrap","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"description":{"$i18n":"threadContext.missing.locale"},"icon":"triangle-alert","title":{"$i18n":"threadContext.noticeTitle"},"toast":true,"tone":"warning","value":"zh-CN"},"id":"toast-locale","type":"Alert"}]},"type":"Stack"},{"config":{"direction":"vertical","maxWidth":"100%","visible":false,"width":"360px"},"id":"toast-viewport-wrap","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"description":{"$i18n":"threadContext.missing.viewportId"},"icon":"triangle-alert","title":{"$i18n":"threadContext.noticeTitle"},"toast":true,"tone":"warning","value":"phone-small"},"id":"toast-viewport","type":"Alert"}]},"type":"Stack"},{"config":{"direction":"vertical","maxWidth":"100%","visible":false,"width":"360px"},"id":"toast-theme-wrap","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"description":{"$i18n":"threadContext.missing.themeId"},"icon":"triangle-alert","title":{"$i18n":"threadContext.noticeTitle"},"toast":true,"tone":"warning","value":"high-contrast"},"id":"toast-theme","type":"Alert"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"RootShell"},"name":"Thread bubble: recorded context and anchor notices","spec":{"accessibility":["The recorded context has a spoken prefix and, for a missing key, says it is no longer in the Workspace, so the state never rests on color; each note and notice is plain text.","After Show in recorded context or Open in current context, the button unmounts and focus stays in the bubble; the switch is announced."],"constraints":["Built only from Adapter Widgets (Stack, Text, Button, Badge, Icon, Avatar, TextInput, Alert); no Widget outside the Adapter catalog.","Each context, notice and note is shown by one Variant; a missing key is flagged in the warning tone without the strike-through of the app, whose accessible text says the key is gone. The bubble keeps the base reply box and Resolve of the Thread bubble View under the notices.","The strings of the app are copied under the same Locale keys; a key or id binds through value, and the toasts are Alerts in the toast look without the app's 10-second timing and placement.","Every visible string is bound with $i18n except identities (Locale, viewport and theme keys, ids, names); en-US and zh-TW keep identical key sets.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["A reader opened a thread of a View: from its pin, from a Comments row, or from a link or the Reviews inbox that carries the thread; the bubble opens over the canvas.","The base state is the header, the label of the Preview context the thread recorded (a Locale, a viewport and a theme, here zh-TW · mobile · dark), one message and the reply box; the Variants add what applies to one thread.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset, one Locale and one theme; the bubble is Workbench chrome, so its text follows the Workbench language and is baked here per Locale. The ids, names and messages are sample content."],"intent":"Show what the thread bubble says about where a thread was made and where it sits, as built from Adapter Widgets only: the Preview context the thread recorded, the offer to see it there or in the reader's own, the notice for a recorded key that no longer exists, and the notes for a thread whose Widget or Variant is gone or whose pin is not on the canvas.","interactionRules":["A thread made on the canvas records each of the Preview's Locale, viewport and theme that is a Workspace-local key, and its header shows only those, as identities in the mono register, with an eye glyph; a thread that records none shows no label and is never muted.","When the recorded context differs from the Preview's current one, the bubble keeps its place, muted: it says Recorded in another Preview context and offers Show in recorded context, which switches the Preview to the recorded members (never the chrome, the Variant or a member the thread does not record).","When a link switched the Preview to the recorded context, the header offers Open in current context, which returns the reader's own context with the thread still open; it changes the Preview only.","A recorded Locale, viewport or theme that no longer exists opens the thread with the default for it, flags the key in the label, and shows a warning toast that names it and says which default is shown; nothing blocks.","A thread whose Widget no longer exists says so and offers Re-anchor, and is kept as it was; a named Variant that no longer exists is listed with a caution; a thread whose pin is not drawn says why in one line: scrolled out, point not visible, not visible in this state, scoped to another Variant (with Switch to), not measurable, not tracked, or the preview reconnecting."],"references":[{"label":"Phase 5 of the closed loop: dogfood coverage of the core surfaces","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/379#discussioncomment-19257377"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"c6c0a104-7b3e-4d19-8a26-3e9d1c0b6a04"}],"requirements":["01a1170f-c11d-7d39-a5ce-cfe9ffdff6ed"]},"variants":{"muted":{"requirements":["01a1170f-c1ae-78fc-98cb-dc8f4b97f98f","01a1170f-c1f7-7e54-8754-c1a047415d4e"],"state":{"ctx-muted-note":{"visible":true},"ctx-open-recorded":{"visible":true}}},"no-recorded-context":{"requirements":["01a1170f-c23d-7318-b035-f84526e4b98f"],"state":{"ctx":{"visible":false}}},"opened-from-link":{"requirements":["01a1170f-c11d-7d39-a5ce-cfe9ffdff6ed"],"state":{"ctx-open-current":{"visible":true}}},"pin-not-measurable":{"requirements":["01a11544-5d39-733d-9581-eccc137f7263"],"state":{"note-hidden":{"visible":false},"note-mapping":{"visible":true},"note-offscreen":{"visible":false}